/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 329 0 R
/T (We start with creating our first chain, namely the prompt template that Phi-3 expects. In the previous chapter, we explored how transformers.pipeline applies the chat template automatically. This is not always the case with other packages and they might need the prompt template to be explicitly defined. With LangChain, we will use chains to create and use a default prompt template. It also serves as a nice hands-on experience with using prompt templates. )
/E (We start with creating our first chain, namely the prompt template that Phi-3 expects. In the previous chapter, we explored how transformers.pipeline applies the chat template automatically. This is not always the case with other packages and they might need the prompt template to be explicitly defined. With LangChain, we will use chains to create and use a default prompt template. It also serves as a nice hands-on experience with using prompt templates. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
