/Title (Thus far, we have created systems that follow a user-defined set of steps to take. One of the most promising concepts in LLMs is their ability to determine the actions they can take. This idea is often called agents, systems that leverage a language model to determine which actions they should take and in what order.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 505 0 R
/Next 609 0 R
>>
endobj
574 0 obj
<<
/Title (For example, LLMs are notoriously bad at mathematical problems and often fail at solving simple math-based tasks but they could do much more if we provide access to a calculator. As illustrated in Figure 7-14, the underlying idea of agents is that they utilize LLMs not only to understand our query but also to decide which tool to use and when.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 505 0 R
/Prev 610 0 R
>>
endobj
