614 0 obj
<<
/Title (In our previous example, we essentially created a chatbot. You could talk to it and it remembers the conversation you had thus far. However, as the size of the conversa tion grows, so does the size of the input prompt until it exceeds the token limit. One method of minimizing the context window is to use the last k conversations instead of maintaining the full chat history. In LangChain, we can use Conversation BufferWindowMemory to decide how many conversations are passed to the input prompt)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 606 0 R
>>
endobj
